RESEARCH INSPIRATION AND ATTRIBUTION
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

This project's architecture, capability taxonomy, and two-stage discovery
protocol are inspired by the following research and initiatives:

1. MIT AI Agent Index (2025)
   Massachusetts Institute of Technology
   URL: https://aiagentindex.mit.edu
   Description: A comprehensive index of AI agents documenting design
   patterns, capabilities, and safety features across 30+ prominent agents.
   Informed our agent card metadata schema and capability categorisation.

2. MIT NANDA Initiative
   Networked Agents and Decentralized AI
   Massachusetts Institute of Technology
   Description: Research on neutral, consortium-governed switchboards for
   cross-organizational agent coordination and federated discovery.
   Informed our federation architecture and registry governance model.

3. MIT Media Lab — Multi-Agent Systems Research
   URL: https://www.media.mit.edu
   Description: Research on multi-agent system coordination patterns.
   Informed our two-stage broker model (discover → connect → disengage).

4. AGNTCY Agent Directory
   URL: https://agntcy.org
   Description: IPFS Kademlia DHT-based routing with OCI-aligned content
   addressing and Sigstore integrity verification.
   Informed our decentralised federation extension design.

5. CapIndex — Open Standard for Agent-Discoverable Capabilities
   URL: https://capindex.dev
   Description: Open standard for capability cards with semantic summaries
   and machine-queryable descriptions.
   Informed our compact capability card and taxonomy code format.

